💭 A program that imports a package which imports another.
💭
💭 Expected: the program links, and prints 11.
💭 What happens: the link fails with undefined references to the inner package's
💭 symbols, and the compiler ends with status 0 all the same. It puts every package on the link line, those
💭 that only another package imports among them, in the reverse of the order it met
💭 them. With static archives a package that comes before the one which needs it is
💭 passed over, and the link fails with undefined references.
💭
💭 Compiling the program with -c and linking by hand, with the archives between
💭 -Wl,--start-group and -Wl,--end-group, works.
